# Cloudflare Pages reads this file from the deploy root and applies these response
# headers. Two concerns matter for a Module Federation remote served cross-origin:
#
# 1. CORS — the Shell is on a DIFFERENT origin (Vercel), so the browser will block
#    fetching this remote's manifest/chunks unless we send Access-Control-Allow-Origin.
#    "*" is fine to start; tighten to the Shell's exact origin once it has a stable URL.
#
# 2. Caching — hashed chunk filenames change on every build, so they're immutable and
#    can be cached forever. mf-manifest.json keeps a STABLE name but its contents change
#    each deploy, so it must NOT be cached or clients would pin to an old remote version.

# Hashed, content-addressed assets: cache forever.
/static/*
  Access-Control-Allow-Origin: *
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=31536000, immutable

# The federation manifest + stats: always revalidate so a new deploy goes live.
/mf-manifest.json
  Access-Control-Allow-Origin: *
  Cache-Control: no-cache

/mf-stats.json
  Access-Control-Allow-Origin: *
  Cache-Control: no-cache
